            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

- Receptacles

- Some windows (Basemet single pane wood window, Master bedroom)

- Wood stove chimney

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <ceilings>At the time of the audit, we estimated the attic insulation to be R-30. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60. </ceilings>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the wood and leaky windows by triple-pane and Energy-star certified units. </windows>
                <VentilationSystem />
            </RURComments>
